[section:MutableBufferSequences Mutable buffer sequences requirements]

A ['mutable buffer sequences] range represents a set of memory regions into
which datagrams may be received by an operation, such as the `receive_multiple`
operation of a datagram socket. Each element describes the memory regions for
one datagram.

A type `X` meets the `MutableBufferSequences` requirements if it satisfies the
requirements of `Destructible` (C++Std [destructible]) and `CopyConstructible`
(C++Std [copyconstructible]), as well as the additional requirements listed
below.

In the table below, `x` denotes a (possibly const) value of type `X`, or of type
`R` if `X` is `std::reference_wrapper<R>`.

[table MutableBufferSequences requirements
  [[expression] [return type] [assertion/note[br]pre/post-condition]]
  [
    [`x.begin()`[br]
     `x.end()`]
    [A type meeting the requirements for forward iterators
     (C++Std \[forward.iterators\]) whose value type meets the
     [link asio.reference.MutableBufferSequence `MutableBufferSequence`]
     requirements.]
    [[half_open_range `x.begin()`,`x.end()`] is a valid range. The range
     may be traversed more than once.]
  ]
]

[endsect]
